  "reason": "Evidence: config_003 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) is the current best at 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1. All major design choices are well-supported: scvi_n200 >> scgpt (0.71 vs 0.54), imagenet_vit_l > resnet50, transformer > avgpool with scvi_n200, multiprofile >> singleprofile, and weighted > concat in every head-to-head comparison. The one remaining untested variation of this optimal architecture is concat fusion with transformer aggregation (config_046). Question: does concat fusion interact differently with transformer aggregation than it does with avgpool, potentially closing or reversing the weighted-vs-concat gap? Rationale: With only 2 experiments left after this one, exploiting the known-best direction is the highest-EV move. config_046 is the only untested configuration that preserves all four 'best' settings (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, multiprofile) while varying the one remaining axis. If it matches or beats 0.725, we confirm the ceiling; if not, we can confidently declare config_003 the final answer with the last experiment. Expected cost: ~3.5–3.7 GPU hours (same transformer + scvi_n200 + ViT-L backbone as config_003; concat vs weighted fusion adds negligible compute), making it a moderate-cost experiment comparable to the current best."
